   "key": "encounter_1",
   "role": "encounter_transcript",
   "label": "Encounter 1 transcript (new-visit)",
   "content": "[S1 E1 Doctor 00:00] Good morning. What brings you in today?\n[S2 E1 Patient 00:03] I have had chest tightness for two days, mostly when I climb stairs.\n[S3 E1 Doctor 00:08] Any allergies to medicines?\n[S4 E1 Patient 00:10] Yes, I am allergic to penicillin. It gives me a rash.\n[S5 E1 Doctor 00:14] And your regular medicines?\n[S6 E1 Patient 00:16] Metformin 500 mg twice daily for my diabetes.\n[S7 E1 Doctor 00:20] Your blood pressure today is 150 over 95. I am sending you for an ECG and a troponin test, then come back to me.",
   "tokens": 319
  },
  {
   "key": "encounter_2",
   "role": "encounter_transcript",
   "label": "Encounter 2 transcript (revisit)",
   "content": "[S8 E2 Doctor 00:00] Welcome back. Your ECG is normal and the troponin is 12, which is normal.\n[S9 E2 Patient 00:06] That is a relief. The tightness is a bit better.\n[S10 E2 Doctor 00:09] Your sugars are high, so I am increasing metformin to 1000 mg twice daily.\n[S11 E2 Doctor 00:15] I am also starting amlodipine 5 mg once daily for the blood pressure. Review in four weeks.",
   "tokens": 243
  }
